# Paid feature source (anything sold rather than given away). The public
# build never ships these — the branch that mounts them is fenced behind the MAKERLAB
# compile-time flag and resolved through `virtual:pro-pack` — but the SOURCE would still be
# readable in a public repo, which is the whole thing people are paying for.
apps/*/src/pro/

# Unreleased apps. This repo is public and it is the live site, so an app in it is an
# announcement — the whole design, before it is finished and before it is decided whether it
# ships free, paid or at all. It stays on disk and stays a pnpm workspace member, so
# `pnpm --filter laser-slot dev` works exactly as it did; it is simply not published yet.
# Add the app back here and to generators.json (with a build + copy step in deploy.yml, or
# the hub card is a 404) on the day it ships.
#
# It was tracked until 2026-08-17, so it is still readable in the history — removing it
# from HEAD hides it from anyone browsing, not from anyone looking.
apps/laser-slot/

# Foldbox ships PRINT-ONLY (2026-08-26). The app is published; its unlaunched CUT half is
# not. `cutPackPlugin` in apps/foldbox/vite.config.ts already keeps these three modules out
# of the default bundle — this keeps them out of the public tree as well, for the same
# reason as `apps/*/src/pro/` above: a finished-but-unlaunched design is an announcement.
#
# Consequence, on purpose: a fresh clone can run `pnpm --filter foldbox build` (print-only,
# what deploy.yml builds) but NOT `build:full`, `build:offline` or `pnpm --filter foldbox
# dev` — all of which run --mode full and resolve `virtual:cut-pack` to cutPack.ts. Use
# `dev:print` (which is what `pnpm dev:foldbox` runs) in a clone. Un-ignore these on the day
# the cut half launches, together with the phase-2 wording already fenced in index.html.
apps/foldbox/src/export/cutFiles.ts
apps/foldbox/src/export/cutPack.ts
apps/foldbox/src/export/lac.ts
# Cut-half working output and fit rigs — real .svg/.dxf cut files and the scratch harnesses
# that produced them. Same fence, one level out.
apps/foldbox/demo/
apps/foldbox/srcfit/
apps/foldbox/testfit/
apps/foldbox/scripts/
apps/foldbox/offline.README.txt
# The full engineering README, which documents both halves — machine tables, kerf, cut order,
# the glued styles. `apps/foldbox/README.md` is the print-only cut-down of it, and is tracked.
apps/foldbox/README.internal.md

